      "Language": "fin",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe a middle-aged patient, in whom a rare subluxation of the costotransversal joint caused a severe axillary pain. Diagnosis was not achieved by imaging studies or electroneuromyography, but instead simply by palpation. A good treatment outcome was obtained by manipulation."},
